feat(console): instrument the fastboot reset path and add SYSTEM_RESET2

FASTBOOT writes the Qualcomm restart reason into IMEM and resets, but the board
still boots normally.  Nothing ever captured the command's own log lines: the
reset did not give the log ring time to drain, and no read-back proved whether
the write stuck.  This change adds measurement, and one alternative reset the
firmware may offer; the proven REBOOT path still uses SYSTEM_RESET unchanged.

  * PSCI_VERSION and PSCI_FEATURES for SYSTEM_RESET and SYSTEM_RESET2 are read
    once at start-up and again on demand (PSCI?).  A feature result of 0 for
    0xC4000012 means the architectural warm reset does not exist on this
    firmware; it is reported as NOT_SUPPORTED rather than replaced with a
    vendor-specific reset type.
  * The IMEM cell is read at start-up, the earliest point this kernel can
    observe what the bootloader left behind.  ABL may have consumed or cleared
    it, so a zero there does not prove the value was lost during reset.
  * FASTBOOT now drains the console log, waits 300 ms, and reads the cell back
    after writing it, so the old value, the new value and the read-back all
    reach the host before the port disappears.
  * FASTBOOT2 performs the same IMEM write and then SYSTEM_RESET2 with
    reset_type 0 (architectural warm reset) and cookie 0 instead of
    PEHaltRestart().  It refuses to reset unless the feature probe returned 1.
    It is a separate command so the original FASTBOOT stays a one-change test.
  * IMEM? is a read-only dump of the cell.

The reset calls live next to SYSTEM_RESET in KebabPlatformExpert.cpp so the
firmware interface keeps one owner; the USB driver only decides when to ask.

